    "question_text": "Describe the human respiratory system and explain how gas exchange occurs.",
    "max_marks": 10,
    "answer_key_text": "The human respiratory system includes the nose, trachea, bronchi, bronchioles, and lungs. Air enters through the nose, passes through the trachea, and reaches the alveoli in the lungs. Gas exchange occurs in the alveoli where oxygen diffuses into the blood and carbon dioxide diffuses out.",
